Chapter: UsbKbdSilent
  cites Works chapter GopUsb
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Works chapter GopRtc
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The ASUS TUF state, on the desk at last: the first keyboard-shaped
 interface completes every interrupt IN with SUCCESS and eight zero
 bytes with a key held, while a DIFFERENT device carries the keys.
 `-hid-root-silent` gives the root keyboard exactly that behaviour and
 moves the injected keys to the hub-attached keyboard; `-hid-keys`
 removes the PS/2 route, so the only way a scancode can reach the
 mailbox is through the second keyboard's own interrupt pipe.

 `got=30` is therefore the fix: bind every boot keyboard, pump them all.
 A walk that stops at the first match waits here forever and answers
 `got=0`. `primary-live=0` beside `peer-live=Y peer-scans=Y` is the
 reading that decides which interface a person is typing on, and it is
 the same e/n pair the desk's top bar and DeskBoot's keyboard hold show
 on the glass.

Section: Test

  peers-line : UsbKbd -> Text
  peers-line (k) =
    "kbd: ok=" & (if k.uk-ok then "1" else "0")
      & " peers=" & show (kbd-peers k)
      & " peer0-route=" & (if kbd-peers k > 0 then show (((kbd-peer k 0).uk-dev).ud-route) else "-")

 The wait is bounded by the RTC rather than by an iteration count: each
 pump costs several VM exits, so a count large enough to cover the key
 timeline in iterations is minutes of wall clock.

  uks-wait : UsbKbd, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  uks-wait (k) (want) (prev) (secs) = act
    sc <- kbd-take k
    now <- rtc-seconds 0
    if sc == want then sc
    else if secs <= 0 then 0
    else if now < 0 then uks-wait k want prev secs
    else if now == prev then uks-wait k want prev secs
    else uks-wait k want now (secs - 1)
  end

  yn : Integer -> Text
  yn (n) = if n > 0 then "Y" else "0"

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    att <- usb-attach
    let k = att.ua-kbd
    in act
      print-line-uni (peers-line k)
      s0 <- rtc-seconds 0
      got <- uks-wait k 30 s0 8
      print-line-uni ("got=" & show got)
      if kbd-peers k > 0 then
        let p = kbd-peer k 0
        in print-line-uni ("primary-live=" & yn (kbd-live k) & " peer-live=" & yn (kbd-live p) & " peer-scans=" & yn (kbd-scans p))
      else print-line-uni ("primary-live=" & yn (kbd-live k) & " peer-live=- peer-scans=-")
    end
  end
